s into more detail about  the spending and it is now saying  specifically that some of that recount  money was used is being used to pay for  Jill Stein  legal troubles related to the Russia  investigation and as some of you know  and as some of you  don't know Jill Stein has been pulled in  to the Russia probe and is suspected of  possible wrong wrongdoing  she has dined with Putin and the  indicted Michael Flynn in Russia  documents have been requested from her  she's had dealings with the United  States Senate Select Committee on  Intelligence and she has not as of yet  been charged with anything but she has  had not insignificant legal expenses  related to this and for a while her  campaign hadn't released an FEC filing  outlining their spending  they now have and it's raising more  questions because the stein campaign  paid the partnership for civil justice  about sixty six thousand dollars in May  and another $31,000 in January and that  is a law firm that is representing Jill  Stein in her dealings to related to the  Russia probe now we don't know for sure  if the hundred thousand paid to them by  the Jill Stein from the Jill Stein  money's were for representing her in the  Russia probe or if they're also  representing her on something else but  we know that they're representing her on  the Russia probe and that payments were  made to them another example nine  thousand dollars went to Miller and  Chevalier which works with Paul Manafort  related to the Russia probe we don't  know if Jill Stein's $10,000 payment to  them was for Russia related stuff but  once again it would appear that way and  of course Jill Stein has every right to  have attorneys for the Russia stuff she  absolutely should everybody deserves to  be represented by attorneys if they are  being investigated but the Stein  campaign has said time and time again  that the money they raise for the  recounts would be held separately and  would be used only for recounts and yet  again it doesn't ap